{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BDZrULS5av4jGPbkoiRNAi","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Test translation guide (Phase 3A)\n2\t\n3\tA focused reference for the C-test → Rust-test translation pass.\n4\t**Read this first.**  It substitutes for grepping `lib.rs` /\n5\t`internal.rs`; you only need to open them when you can't find an\n6\tanswer here.\n7\t\n8\t---\n9\t\n10\t## Operating mandate\n11\t\n12\t* **Translate every C test body faithfully.**  No `todo!(\"entry_fn\")`\n13\t  placeholders.  The body should reproduce what the C body does.\n14\t* **Compile-not-pass is the gate.**  Tests will panic on the first\n15\t  `todo!()` they hit inside a Phase-1-stubbed API.  That's expected\n16\t  and the user explicitly approved it.\n17\t* **Use the Rust public API as designed.**  If the canonical method\n18\t  doesn't exist yet, call the *intended* method anyway — the\n19\t  resulting compile error documents the API Phase 4 must supply.\n20\t* **No `unsafe`.**  No edits outside `rs/fq/src/tests/` and\n21\t  `rs/fq/tests/fixtures/`.\n22\t* The build gate is `cargo fmt && cargo test --no-run && cargo\n23\t  clippy --tests --all-features -- -D warnings`.  Iterate until all\n24\t  three are clean.\n25\t\n26\t---\n27\t\n28\t## Crate map (where APIs live)\n29\t\n30\t| Module | Surface |\n31\t|---|---|\n32\t| `crate::lib` (re-exported at root) | public API: `Quic`, `Connection`, `ConnectionId`, `Error`, `Result`, `Instant`, `Duration`, `VERSION`, `MAX_PACKET_SIZE`, `RESET_SECRET_SIZE`, `Alpn`, `State`, `PacketContext`, `PmtudPolicy`, `SpinbitVersion`, `LossbitVersion`, `PathStatus`, `CloseReason`, `CongestionAlgorithm`, callbacks (`StreamDataCallback`, `AlpnSelect`, `ConnectionIdCallback`, `Fuzz`, `StreamDirectReceive`, `CongestionControl`) |\n33\t| `crate::internal` | internal types touched by tests: `Path`, `PacketHeader`, `PacketType`, `Epoch`, `SackList`, `SackItem`, `Pacing`, `MiscFrameHeader`, `Tuple`, `LocalConnectionId`, `RemoteConnectionId`, `StreamDataNode`, `Packet`, `RegisteredToken`, `StoredTicket`, `StoredToken`, `IssuedTicket`, `MinMaxRtt`, `NewRenoSimState`; helpers like `parse_16/24/32/64`, `format_16/24/32/64`, `varint_encode/decode`, `get_packet_number64`, `create_long_header`, `create_packet_header`, `seed_bandwidth` |\n34\t| `crate::tp` | `TransportParameter`, `TransportParameters`, `PreferredAddress`, `VersionNegotiation`, `TransportParameter0RttKind`, `NB_TP_0RTT` |\n35\t| `crate::frames` | `FrameType`, `FrameType::name(u64) -> Option<&'static str>` |\n36\t| `crate::stream` | `StreamId(pub u64)`, `Direction`, `Role` + `is_client`, `is_bidir`, `is_local`, `from_parts`, `rank`, `kind`, `next_with_same_kind` |\n37\t| `crate::errors` | `InternalError` (picoquic-internal codes), `TransportError` (RFC 9000 §20), `transport_crypto_error(alert: u8)`, `InternalError::name(u64)` |\n38\t| `crate::bytestream` | `ByteStream<'a>`, `ByteStreamBuf`, `BYTESTREAM_MAX_BUFFER_SIZE` |\n39\t| `crate::splay` | `SplayTree<K, V>`, `SplayToken` |\n40\t| `crate::hash` | `HashTable`, `HashToken`, `HashItem` |\n41\t| `crate::arena` | `Arena<T>`, `Token<T>` |\n42\t| `crate::siphash` | `siphash(input: &[u8], key: &[u8; 16]) -> u64` |\n43\t| `crate::utils` | `uint8_to_str`, `constant_time_memcmp`, `set_preferred_address` |\n44\t| `crate::tls` | `Session`, `ClientConfig`, `ServerConfig`, `TlsBackend`, `PacketKey`, `HeaderKey`, `Keys`, `KeyPair`, `TlsCallbacks` |\n45\t| `crate::tls_api` | TLS handshake glue: `Aes128EcbContext`, `setup_initial_master_secret`, `setup_initial_secrets`, `rotate_app_secret`, `setup_test_aead_context`, `pn_enc_create_for_test`, `create_retry_protection_context`, `encode_retry_protection`, `verify_retry_protection`, `hash_create`, `hash_get_length`, `QUIC_AEAD_TAG_LEN` |\n46\t| `crate::lb` | LB CID config: `Config`, `ConnectionIdContext`, `ConnectionIdMethod`, `RotationBits` |\n47\t| `crate::config` | demo-app `Config`, `OptionId`, `Config::option_letters() -> String`, `Config::parse_command_line`, `Config::set_option` |\n48\t| `crate::logger` | `Logger` (backend trait), `Log` (per-Connection dispatch trait) |\n49\t| `crate::binlog` | `Binlog` (per-Connection trait), free fns `pdu`, `packet`, `tls_ticket` (file-only writers), `LogEventType`, `Quic::set_binlog`, `Quic::enable_binlog` |\n50\t| `crate::qlog` | `Quic::set_qlog` |\n51\t| `crate::header_protection` | `AesHeaderProtector<C>`, `AesHeaderKey<C>`, `ChaCha20HeaderProtector`, `ChaCha20HeaderKey` |\n52\t| `crate::cc_common` | `MIN_MAX_RTT_SCOPE`, `HYSTART_PP_*`, `MinMaxRtt`, `NewRenoSimState`, `ConnectionCc` (trait on Connection), `PathCc` (trait on Path) |\n53\t| `crate::socks` / `crate::socks_socket2` | `Socket` trait, `ServerSockets<S>`, `Socket2Udp` |\n54\t| `crate::packet_loop` | `LoopParam`, `LoopEvent`, `PacketLoopCbFn`, `NetworkThreadCtx`, `SocketCtx<S>` |\n55\t| `crate::sys::picotls` / `crate::sys::openssl` | TLS backends |\n56\t| `crate::tests::util` | test infrastructure (see below) |\n57\t| `crate::tests::dualq` | DualQ AQM `TestAqm` impl |\n58\t\n59\t---\n60\t\n61\t## Constructors & key signatures\n62\t\n63\t```rust\n64\t// Top-level QUIC context.\n65\tQuic::new(\n66\t    max_nb_connections: u32,\n67\t    cert_file_name: Option<&str>,\n68\t    key_file_name: Option<&str>,\n69\t    cert_root_file_name: Option<&str>,\n70\t    default_alpn: Option<&str>,\n71\t    default_callback: Option<Box<dyn StreamDataCallback>>,\n72\t    cnx_id_callback: Option<Box<dyn ConnectionIdCallback>>,\n73\t    reset_seed: [u8; RESET_SECRET_SIZE],\n74\t    current_time: Instant,\n75\t    ticket_file_name: Option<&str>,\n76\t    ticket_encryption_key: Option<&[u8]>,\n77\t) -> Option<Box<Quic>>;\n78\t\n79\t// Per-connection.\n80\tQuic::create_connection(\n81\t    &mut self,\n82\t    initial_cnx_id: ConnectionId,\n83\t    remote_cnx_id: ConnectionId,\n84\t    addr_to: Option<&SocketAddr>,\n85\t    start_time: Instant,\n86\t    preferred_version: u32,\n87\t    sni: Option<&str>,\n88\t    alpn: Option<&str>,\n89\t    client_mode: bool,\n90\t) -> Option<&mut Connection>;\n91\t\n92\tQuic::create_client_connection(\n93\t    &mut self,\n94\t    addr: &SocketAddr,\n95\t    start_time: Instant,\n96\t    preferred_version: u32,\n97\t    sni: Option<&str>,\n98\t    alpn: Option<&str>,\n99\t    callback: Option<Box<dyn StreamDataCallback>>,\n100\t) -> Option<&mut Connection>;\n101\t\n102\tConnection::start_client(&mut self) -> Result<(), Error>;\n103\tConnection::close(&mut self, application_reason_code: u64) -> Result<(), Error>;\n104\tConnection::tls_negotiated_alpn(&self) -> Alpn;\n105\tConnection::tls_sni(&self) -> Option<&str>;\n106\tConnection::close_reason(&self) -> Option<CloseReason>;\n107\t\n108\t// ConnectionId.\n109\tConnectionId::clone_from_slice(bytes: &[u8]) -> Option<Self>;\n110\tConnectionId::with_size(len: usize) -> Option<Self>;\n111\tConnectionId::as_bytes(&self) -> &[u8];\n112\tConnectionId::as_bytes_mut(&mut self) -> &mut [u8];\n113\tConnectionId::len(&self) -> usize;\n114\tConnectionId::is_empty(&self) -> bool;\n115\t```\n116\t\n117\tTime and duration are `fugit::Instant<u64, 1, 1_000_000>` and\n118\t`fugit::Duration<u64, 1, 1_000_000>` — microseconds.  Construct\n119\twith `Instant::from_ticks(usec)` / `Duration::from_ticks(usec)`.\n120\t\n121\t---\n122\t\n123\t## Free fns vs methods — both shapes exist\n124\t\n125\tPhase 1A's \"free function on `&mut T` becomes a method on `T`\" rule\n126\twas applied unevenly.  **About half** of the C `picoquic_xxx(cnx, …)`\n127\tfunctions live in `crate::internal` as free functions of the same\n128\tshape, *not* as methods on `Connection`.  When you can't find a\n129\tmethod, **also check for the free-function form**:\n130\t\n131\t```text\n132\t# Search both shapes:\n133\tgrep -nE \"fn xxx\" rs/fq/src/internal.rs\n134\tgrep -nE \"^pub fn xxx\" rs/fq/src/internal.rs\n135\t```\n136\t\n137\t### SACK / ACK frame surface (canonical example)\n138\t\n139\tThese are all in `crate::internal` as free functions:\n140\t\n141\t```rust\n142\tpub fn is_ack_needed(connection: &mut Connection, current_time: Instant,\n143\t    next_wake_time: &mut Instant, packet_context: PacketContext,\n144\t    is_opportunistic: i32) -> bool;\n145\t\n146\tpub fn is_pn_already_received(connection: &mut Connection,\n147\t    packet_context: PacketContext,\n148\t    local_connection_id: Option<LocalConnectionIdToken>,\n149\t    pn: u64) -> i32;\n150\t\n151\tpub fn record_pn_received(connection: &mut Connection,\n152\t    packet_context: PacketContext,\n153\t    local_connection_id: Option<LocalConnectionIdToken>,\n154\t    pn: u64, current_time: Instant) -> i32;\n155\t\n156\tpub fn set_ack_needed(connection: &mut Connection, current_time: Instant,\n157\t    packet_context: PacketContext, path_x: &mut Path,\n158\t    out_of_order: i32);\n159\t\n160\tpub fn format_ack_frame<'a>(connection: &mut Connection,\n161\t    bytes: &'a mut [u8], more_data: &mut i32,\n162\t    current_time: Instant, packet_context: PacketContext,\n163\t    is_opportunistic: i32) -> Option<&'a mut [u8]>;\n164\t\n165\tpub fn create_local_cnx_id(connection: &mut Connection,\n166\t    path_id: u64, suggested_value: Option<&ConnectionId>,\n167\t    sequence_offset: u64) -> Option<LocalConnectionIdToken>;\n168\t```\n169\t\n170\t### Other clusters of free functions to know about\n171\t\n172\t- **Frame format/skip/parse:** `skip_frame`, `parse_frame`,\n173\t  `format_*_frame` for each frame type (`format_max_data_frame`,\n174\t  `format_path_challenge_frame`, etc.) — all free fns.\n175\t- **Tuple/path lifecycle:** `create_local_cnx_id`,\n176\t  `find_or_create_remote_connection_id_stash`,\n177\t  `stash_remote_connection_id`, etc.\n178\t- **Retransmit queue:** `queue_for_retransmit`,\n179\t  `dequeue_retransmit_packet`, `dequeue_retransmitted_packet`.\n180\t- **Bandwidth:** `seed_bandwidth`, `update_path_rtt`,\n181\t  `current_retransmit_timer`.\n182\t- **Integer / varint:** `parse_16/24/32/64`, `format_16/24/32/64`,\n183\t  `varint_encode`, `varint_decode`, `varint_skip`,\n184\t  `frames_varint_decode`, `frames_varint_skip`.\n185\t\n186\tIf you don't find an API after the first one or two greps,\n187\t*assume it's a free function in `internal.rs`* and search there\n188\twithout the `impl X` qualifier.\n189\t\n190\t---\n191\t\n192\t## Translation conventions (apply uniformly)\n193\t\n194\t| C pattern | Rust translation |\n195\t|---|---|\n196\t| `picoquic_quic_t* quic` | `&mut Quic` (or `Box<Quic>` when owning) |\n197\t| `picoquic_cnx_t* cnx` | `&mut Connection` (no `Cnx`) |\n198\t| `picoquic_path_t* path_x` | `&mut Path` |\n199\t| `picoquic_connection_id_t cid` | `ConnectionId` (Copy) |\n200\t| `int` return code (0 / -1 / errno) | `Result<T, crate::Error>` |\n201\t| `int` boolean flag | `bool` |\n202\t| `void* callback_ctx` | folds into trait implementor's state |\n203\t| `void (*fn_ptr)(...)` | `Box<dyn Trait>` |\n204\t| `(uint8_t* buf, size_t len)` pair | `&[u8]` (read) or `&mut [u8]` (write) |\n205\t| `(NULL, 0)` slice sentinel | empty Rust slice |\n206\t| `(struct sockaddr*)` | `&core::net::SocketAddr` |\n207\t| `uint64_t` microsecond timestamp | `Instant` |\n208\t| `uint64_t` microsecond interval | `Duration` |\n209\t| `picoquic_xxx_yyy_zzz` | `xxx_yyy_zzz` (drop prefix) |\n210\t| `cnx_id` / `cid` | `connection_id` |\n211\t| `cnx` (in identifiers) | `connection` |\n212\t\n213\t`assert_eq!` / `assert!` over the C `if (...) ret = -1` pattern.\n214\tUse `?` propagation on `Result` returns.  Don't transcribe goto-style\n215\tret tracking — that's a C quirk.\n216\t\n217\t---\n218\t\n219\t## Test-helper surface (`crate::tests::util`)\n220\t\n221\tAvailable test-only utilities (most are still `todo!()` until Phase 4):\n222\t\n223\t```rust\n224\tpub fn test_random(random_context: &mut u64) -> u64;\n225\tpub fn test_random_bytes(random_context: &mut u64, bytes: &mut [u8]);\n226\tpub fn test_uniform_random(random_context: &mut u64, rnd_max: u64) -> u64;\n227\tpub fn test_gauss_random(random_context: &mut u64) -> f64;\n228\tpub fn test_poisson_random(random_context: &mut u64, exp_minus_lambda_2_30: u64) -> u64;\n229\t\n230\tpub struct TestSimPacket { /* simulator packet */ }\n231\tpub struct TestSimLink { /* in-process sim link */ }\n232\tpub trait TestAqm;            // active queue management vtable\n233\tpub enum JitterMode;\n234\t```\n235\t\n236\tPlus certificate-fixture path constants (`TEST_FILE_SERVER_CERT`,\n237\t`TEST_FILE_SERVER_KEY`, `TEST_FILE_CERT_STORE`, `TEST_SNI`, etc.)\n238\tthat translate the picoquictest globals.\n239\t\n240\t**When adding helpers:** if more than one test file needs the\n241\thelper, put it in `tests/util.rs`.  Heavy connection-setup helpers\n242\t(`tls_api_init_ctx`, `picoquic_test_set_minimal_cnx`) go here.\n243\tKeep one canonical name per helper — if you find yourself defining\n244\t`default_quic` or similar in multiple test files, refactor to\n245\t`tests/util.rs`.\n246\t\n247\t---\n248\t\n249\t## Common patterns\n250\t\n251\t### Minimal Quic context\n252\t\n253\t```rust\n254\tfn default_quic() -> Option<Box<Quic>> {\n255\t    Quic::new(\n256\t        8, None, None, None, None, None, None,\n257\t        [0u8; RESET_SECRET_SIZE],\n258\t        Instant::from_ticks(0),\n259\t        None, None,\n260\t    )\n261\t}\n262\t```\n263\t\n264\t### Known-answer table test\n265\t\n266\t```rust\n267\t#[test]\n268\tfn varint() {\n269\t    let cases = [\n270\t        Case { encoding: [...], length: 1, decoded: 0 },\n271\t        // ...\n272\t    ];\n273\t    for case in &cases {\n274\t        // exercise encoder, decoder; assert results\n275\t    }\n276\t}\n277\t```\n278\t\n279\t### Connection-lifecycle test\n280\t\n281\tThe C `tls_api_init_ctx*` family creates a server `Quic`, a\n282\tclient `Quic`, plumbs them via the simulator, and runs a\n283\thandshake loop.  Until those helpers land in `tests/util.rs`\n284\t(Phase 3A may add them), translate as:\n285\t\n286\t```rust\n287\t#[test]\n288\tfn xxx() {\n289\t    let mut server_quic = default_quic().expect(\"server quic\");\n290\t    let mut client_quic = default_quic().expect(\"client quic\");\n291\t    // ... the C body ...\n292\t    todo!(\"tls_api connection-loop helper not yet ported\")  // only as a last resort\n293\t}\n294\t```\n295\t\n296\tPrefer translating the body in full — the panic happens\n297\tnaturally inside `Quic::new` or whatever else is `todo!()`.\n298\t\n299\t### Frame parse / skip table\n300\t\n301\t`crate::internal::skip_frame(buffer: &[u8]) -> Option<(usize, bool)>`\n302\t(or whatever the analogous Rust signature ends up being — call\n303\tthe intended method and let the compile-error / panic document).\n304\t\n305\t---\n306\t\n307\t## Idioms to avoid\n308\t\n309\t* **Don't reach into private fields.**  C tests routinely\n310\t  do `cnx->ack_ctx[pc].sack_list`; the Rust `Connection`\n311\t  struct's fields aren't `pub` from outside `crate::internal`.\n312\t  Use the public method API or surface a comment that the\n313\t  translation needs an accessor.\n314\t* **Don't use `unsafe`.**\n315\t* **Don't use `panic!` where `assert_eq!` / `assert!` work.**\n316\t* **Don't transcribe C goto-ret tracking.**  Use early returns or\n317\t  `?` propagation.\n318\t* **Don't add `#[cfg(target_os = \"linux\")]` etc.** unless the C\n319\t  body itself is OS-specific.\n320\t* **Don't translate `picoquic_test_compare_text_files` golden-file\n321\t  tests** without copying the reference file to `rs/fq/tests/fixtures/`\n322\t  first.  Reach the path via\n323\t  `concat!(env!(\"CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR\"), \"/tests/fixtures/<name>\")`.\n324\t\n325\t---\n326\t\n327\t## Known stubbed surface\n328\t\n329\tMost `Quic` / `Connection` / `Path` methods have signatures only —\n330\ttheir bodies are `todo!()`.  Tests will panic on the first call.\n331\tDon't try to verify behaviour against a working impl; the test is\n332\ta forward-looking spec for Phase 4.\n333\t\n334\tFunctions with **real bodies** today (will pass tests against\n335\tthem):\n336\t\n337\t* `crate::VERSION` (constant)\n338\t* `crate::internal::parse_16/24/32/64`, `format_16/24/32/64`\n339\t* `crate::ConnectionId::{as_bytes, len, is_empty}`\n340\t* `crate::stream::StreamId::{is_client, is_bidir, from_parts,\n341\t  rank, kind, next_with_same_kind}`\n342\t* `crate::frames::FrameType` discriminants (the variants exist,\n343\t  even if `name()` is `todo!()`)\n344\t* `crate::errors::{InternalError, TransportError}` discriminants\n345\t* `crate::tests::util::TestSimPacket` / `TestSimLink` types\n346\t  (signatures only)\n347\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cb85c5eb-b826-43b9-84a4-4be9b46756f2","uuid":"8cd2a791-eef6-4a4f-9230-d48d0c000aa1","timestamp":"2026-05-05T11:45:09.568Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/richbarn/Projects/picoquic/xlate/test_translation_guide.md","content":"# Test translation guide (Phase 3A)\n\nA focused reference for the C-test → Rust-test translation pass.\n**Read this first.**  It substitutes for grepping `lib.rs` /\n`internal.rs`; you only need to open them when you can't find an\nanswer here.\n\n---\n\n## Operating mandate\n\n* **Translate every C test body faithfully.**  No `todo!(\"entry_fn\")`\n  placeholders.  The body should reproduce what the C body does.\n* **Compile-not-pass is the gate.**  Tests will panic on the first\n  `todo!()` they hit inside a Phase-1-stubbed API.  That's expected\n  and the user explicitly approved it.\n* **Use the Rust public API as designed.**  If the canonical method\n  doesn't exist yet, call the *intended* method anyway — the\n  resulting compile error documents the API Phase 4 must supply.\n* **No `unsafe`.**  No edits outside `rs/fq/src/tests/` and\n  `rs/fq/tests/fixtures/`.\n* The build gate is `cargo fmt && cargo test --no-run && cargo\n  clippy --tests --all-features -- -D warnings`.  Iterate until all\n  three are clean.\n\n---\n\n## Crate map (where APIs live)\n\n| Module | Surface |\n|---|---|\n| `crate::lib` (re-exported at root) | public API: `Quic`, `Connection`, `ConnectionId`, `Error`, `Result`, `Instant`, `Duration`, `VERSION`, `MAX_PACKET_SIZE`, `RESET_SECRET_SIZE`, `Alpn`, `State`, `PacketContext`, `PmtudPolicy`, `SpinbitVersion`, `LossbitVersion`, `PathStatus`, `CloseReason`, `CongestionAlgorithm`, callbacks (`StreamDataCallback`, `AlpnSelect`, `ConnectionIdCallback`, `Fuzz`, `StreamDirectReceive`, `CongestionControl`) |\n| `crate::internal` | internal types touched by tests: `Path`, `PacketHeader`, `PacketType`, `Epoch`, `SackList`, `SackItem`, `Pacing`, `MiscFrameHeader`, `Tuple`, `LocalConnectionId`, `RemoteConnectionId`, `StreamDataNode`, `Packet`, `RegisteredToken`, `StoredTicket`, `StoredToken`, `IssuedTicket`, `MinMaxRtt`, `NewRenoSimState`; helpers like `parse_16/24/32/64`, `format_16/24/32/64`, `varint_encode/decode`, `get_packet_number64`, `create_long_header`, `create_packet_header`, `seed_bandwidth` |\n| `crate::tp` | `TransportParameter`, `TransportParameters`, `PreferredAddress`, `VersionNegotiation`, `TransportParameter0RttKind`, `NB_TP_0RTT` |\n| `crate::frames` | `FrameType`, `FrameType::name(u64) -> Option<&'static str>` |\n| `crate::stream` | `StreamId(pub u64)`, `Direction`, `Role` + `is_client`, `is_bidir`, `is_local`, `from_parts`, `rank`, `kind`, `next_with_same_kind` |\n| `crate::errors` | `InternalError` (picoquic-internal codes), `TransportError` (RFC 9000 §20), `transport_crypto_error(alert: u8)`, `InternalError::name(u64)` |\n| `crate::bytestream` | `ByteStream<'a>`, `ByteStreamBuf`, `BYTESTREAM_MAX_BUFFER_SIZE` |\n| `crate::splay` | `SplayTree<K, V>`, `SplayToken` |\n| `crate::hash` | `HashTable`, `HashToken`, `HashItem` |\n| `crate::arena` | `Arena<T>`, `Token<T>` |\n| `crate::siphash` | `siphash(input: &[u8], key: &[u8; 16]) -> u64` |\n| `crate::utils` | `uint8_to_str`, `constant_time_memcmp`, `set_preferred_address` |\n| `crate::tls` | `Session`, `ClientConfig`, `ServerConfig`, `TlsBackend`, `PacketKey`, `HeaderKey`, `Keys`, `KeyPair`, `TlsCallbacks` |\n| `crate::tls_api` | TLS handshake glue: `Aes128EcbContext`, `setup_initial_master_secret`, `setup_initial_secrets`, `rotate_app_secret`, `setup_test_aead_context`, `pn_enc_create_for_test`, `create_retry_protection_context`, `encode_retry_protection`, `verify_retry_protection`, `hash_create`, `hash_get_length`, `QUIC_AEAD_TAG_LEN` |\n| `crate::lb` | LB CID config: `Config`, `ConnectionIdContext`, `ConnectionIdMethod`, `RotationBits` |\n| `crate::config` | demo-app `Config`, `OptionId`, `Config::option_letters() -> String`, `Config::parse_command_line`, `Config::set_option` |\n| `crate::logger` | `Logger` (backend trait), `Log` (per-Connection dispatch trait) |\n| `crate::binlog` | `Binlog` (per-Connection trait), free fns `pdu`, `packet`, `tls_ticket` (file-only writers), `LogEventType`, `Quic::set_binlog`, `Quic::enable_binlog` |\n| `crate::qlog` | `Quic::set_qlog` |\n| `crate::header_protection` | `AesHeaderProtector<C>`, `AesHeaderKey<C>`, `ChaCha20HeaderProtector`, `ChaCha20HeaderKey` |\n| `crate::cc_common` | `MIN_MAX_RTT_SCOPE`, `HYSTART_PP_*`, `MinMaxRtt`, `NewRenoSimState`, `ConnectionCc` (trait on Connection), `PathCc` (trait on Path) |\n| `crate::socks` / `crate::socks_socket2` | `Socket` trait, `ServerSockets<S>`, `Socket2Udp` |\n| `crate::packet_loop` | `LoopParam`, `LoopEvent`, `PacketLoopCbFn`, `NetworkThreadCtx`, `SocketCtx<S>` |\n| `crate::sys::picotls` / `crate::sys::openssl` | TLS backends |\n| `crate::tests::util` | test infrastructure (see below) |\n| `crate::tests::dualq` | DualQ AQM `TestAqm` impl |\n\n---\n\n## Constructors & key signatures\n\n```rust\n// Top-level QUIC context.\nQuic::new(\n    max_nb_connections: u32,\n    cert_file_name: Option<&str>,\n    key_file_name: Option<&str>,\n    cert_root_file_name: Option<&str>,\n    default_alpn: Option<&str>,\n    default_callback: Option<Box<dyn StreamDataCallback>>,\n    cnx_id_callback: Option<Box<dyn ConnectionIdCallback>>,\n    reset_seed: [u8; RESET_SECRET_SIZE],\n    current_time: Instant,\n    ticket_file_name: Option<&str>,\n    ticket_encryption_key: Option<&[u8]>,\n) -> Option<Box<Quic>>;\n\n// Per-connection.\nQuic::create_connection(\n    &mut self,\n    initial_cnx_id: ConnectionId,\n    remote_cnx_id: ConnectionId,\n    addr_to: Option<&SocketAddr>,\n    start_time: Instant,\n    preferred_version: u32,\n    sni: Option<&str>,\n    alpn: Option<&str>,\n    client_mode: bool,\n) -> Option<&mut Connection>;\n\nQuic::create_client_connection(\n    &mut self,\n    addr: &SocketAddr,\n    start_time: Instant,\n    preferred_version: u32,\n    sni: Option<&str>,\n    alpn: Option<&str>,\n    callback: Option<Box<dyn StreamDataCallback>>,\n) -> Option<&mut Connection>;\n\nConnection::start_client(&mut self) -> Result<(), Error>;\nConnection::close(&mut self, application_reason_code: u64) -> Result<(), Error>;\nConnection::tls_negotiated_alpn(&self) -> Alpn;\nConnection::tls_sni(&self) -> Option<&str>;\nConnection::close_reason(&self) -> Option<CloseReason>;\n\n// ConnectionId.\nConnectionId::clone_from_slice(bytes: &[u8]) -> Option<Self>;\nConnectionId::with_size(len: usize) -> Option<Self>;\nConnectionId::as_bytes(&self) -> &[u8];\nConnectionId::as_bytes_mut(&mut self) -> &mut [u8];\nConnectionId::len(&self) -> usize;\nConnectionId::is_empty(&self) -> bool;\n```\n\nTime and duration are `fugit::Instant<u64, 1, 1_000_000>` and\n`fugit::Duration<u64, 1, 1_000_000>` — microseconds.  Construct\nwith `Instant::from_ticks(usec)` / `Duration::from_ticks(usec)`.\n\n---\n\n## Free fns vs methods — both shapes exist\n\nPhase 1A's \"free function on `&mut T` becomes a method on `T`\" rule\nwas applied unevenly.  **About half** of the C `picoquic_xxx(cnx, …)`\nfunctions live in `crate::internal` as free functions of the same\nshape, *not* as methods on `Connection`.  When you can't find a\nmethod, **also check for the free-function form**:\n\n```text\n# Search both shapes:\ngrep -nE \"fn xxx\" rs/fq/src/internal.rs\ngrep -nE \"^pub fn xxx\" rs/fq/src/internal.rs\n```\n\n### SACK / ACK frame surface (canonical example)\n\nThese are all in `crate::internal` as free functions:\n\n```rust\npub fn is_ack_needed(connection: &mut Connection, current_time: Instant,\n    next_wake_time: &mut Instant, packet_context: PacketContext,\n    is_opportunistic: i32) -> bool;\n\npub fn is_pn_already_received(connection: &mut Connection,\n    packet_context: PacketContext,\n    local_connection_id: Option<LocalConnectionIdToken>,\n    pn: u64) -> i32;\n\npub fn record_pn_received(connection: &mut Connection,\n    packet_context: PacketContext,\n    local_connection_id: Option<LocalConnectionIdToken>,\n    pn: u64, current_time: Instant) -> i32;\n\npub fn set_ack_needed(connection: &mut Connection, current_time: Instant,\n    packet_context: PacketContext, path_x: &mut Path,\n    out_of_order: i32);\n\npub fn format_ack_frame<'a>(connection: &mut Connection,\n    bytes: &'a mut [u8], more_data: &mut i32,\n    current_time: Instant, packet_context: PacketContext,\n    is_opportunistic: i32) -> Option<&'a mut [u8]>;\n\npub fn create_local_cnx_id(connection: &mut Connection,\n    path_id: u64, suggested_value: Option<&ConnectionId>,\n    sequence_offset: u64) -> Option<LocalConnectionIdToken>;\n```\n\n### Other clusters of free functions to know about\n\n- **Frame format/skip/parse:** `skip_frame`, `parse_frame`,\n  `format_*_frame` for each frame type (`format_max_data_frame`,\n  `format_path_challenge_frame`, etc.) — all free fns.\n- **Tuple/path lifecycle:** `create_local_cnx_id`,\n  `find_or_create_remote_connection_id_stash`,\n  `stash_remote_connection_id`, etc.\n- **Retransmit queue:** `queue_for_retransmit`,\n  `dequeue_retransmit_packet`, `dequeue_retransmitted_packet`.\n- **Bandwidth:** `seed_bandwidth`, `update_path_rtt`,\n  `current_retransmit_timer`.\n- **Integer / varint:** `parse_16/24/32/64`, `format_16/24/32/64`,\n  `varint_encode`, `varint_decode`, `varint_skip`,\n  `frames_varint_decode`, `frames_varint_skip`.\n\nIf you don't find an API after the first one or two greps,\n*assume it's a free function in `internal.rs`* and search there\nwithout the `impl X` qualifier.\n\n---\n\n## Translation conventions (apply uniformly)\n\n| C pattern | Rust translation |\n|---|---|\n| `picoquic_quic_t* quic` | `&mut Quic` (or `Box<Quic>` when owning) |\n| `picoquic_cnx_t* cnx` | `&mut Connection` (no `Cnx`) |\n| `picoquic_path_t* path_x` | `&mut Path` |\n| `picoquic_connection_id_t cid` | `ConnectionId` (Copy) |\n| `int` return code (0 / -1 / errno) | `Result<T, crate::Error>` |\n| `int` boolean flag | `bool` |\n| `void* callback_ctx` | folds into trait implementor's state |\n| `void (*fn_ptr)(...)` | `Box<dyn Trait>` |\n| `(uint8_t* buf, size_t len)` pair | `&[u8]` (read) or `&mut [u8]` (write) |\n| `(NULL, 0)` slice sentinel | empty Rust slice |\n| `(struct sockaddr*)` | `&core::net::SocketAddr` |\n| `uint64_t` microsecond timestamp | `Instant` |\n| `uint64_t` microsecond interval | `Duration` |\n| `picoquic_xxx_yyy_zzz` | `xxx_yyy_zzz` (drop prefix) |\n| `cnx_id` / `cid` | `connection_id` |\n| `cnx` (in identifiers) | `connection` |\n\n`assert_eq!` / `assert!` over the C `if (...) ret = -1` pattern.\nUse `?` propagation on `Result` returns.  Don't transcribe goto-style\nret tracking — that's a C quirk.\n\n---\n\n## Test-helper surface (`crate::tests::util`)\n\nAvailable test-only utilities (most are still `todo!()` until Phase 4):\n\n```rust\npub fn test_random(random_context: &mut u64) -> u64;\npub fn test_random_bytes(random_context: &mut u64, bytes: &mut [u8]);\npub fn test_uniform_random(random_context: &mut u64, rnd_max: u64) -> u64;\npub fn test_gauss_random(random_context: &mut u64) -> f64;\npub fn test_poisson_random(random_context: &mut u64, exp_minus_lambda_2_30: u64) -> u64;\n\npub struct TestSimPacket { /* simulator packet */ }\npub struct TestSimLink { /* in-process sim link */ }\npub trait TestAqm;            // active queue management vtable\npub enum JitterMode;\n```\n\nPlus certificate-fixture path constants (`TEST_FILE_SERVER_CERT`,\n`TEST_FILE_SERVER_KEY`, `TEST_FILE_CERT_STORE`, `TEST_SNI`, etc.)\nthat translate the picoquictest globals.\n\n**When adding helpers:** if more than one test file needs the\nhelper, put it in `tests/util.rs`.  Heavy connection-setup helpers\n(`tls_api_init_ctx`, `picoquic_test_set_minimal_cnx`) go here.\nKeep one canonical name per helper — if you find yourself defining\n`default_quic` or similar in multiple test files, refactor to\n`tests/util.rs`.\n\n---\n\n## Common patterns\n\n### Minimal Quic context\n\n```rust\nfn default_quic() -> Option<Box<Quic>> {\n    Quic::new(\n        8, None, None, None, None, None, None,\n        [0u8; RESET_SECRET_SIZE],\n        Instant::from_ticks(0),\n        None, None,\n    )\n}\n```\n\n### Known-answer table test\n\n```rust\n#[test]\nfn varint() {\n    let cases = [\n        Case { encoding: [...], length: 1, decoded: 0 },\n        // ...\n    ];\n    for case in &cases {\n        // exercise encoder, decoder; assert results\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Connection-lifecycle test\n\nThe C `tls_api_init_ctx*` family creates a server `Quic`, a\nclient `Quic`, plumbs them via the simulator, and runs a\nhandshake loop.  Until those helpers land in `tests/util.rs`\n(Phase 3A may add them), translate as:\n\n```rust\n#[test]\nfn xxx() {\n    let mut server_quic = default_quic().expect(\"server quic\");\n    let mut client_quic = default_quic().expect(\"client quic\");\n    // ... the C body ...\n    todo!(\"tls_api connection-loop helper not yet ported\")  // only as a last resort\n}\n```\n\nPrefer translating the body in full — the panic happens\nnaturally inside `Quic::new` or whatever else is `todo!()`.\n\n### Frame parse / skip table\n\n`crate::internal::skip_frame(buffer: &[u8]) -> Option<(usize, bool)>`\n(or whatever the analogous Rust signature ends up being — call\nthe intended method and let the compile-error / panic document).\n\n---\n\n## Idioms to avoid\n\n* **Don't reach into private fields.**  C tests routinely\n  do `cnx->ack_ctx[pc].sack_list`; the Rust `Connection`\n  struct's fields aren't `pub` from outside `crate::internal`.\n  Use the public method API or surface a comment that the\n  translation needs an accessor.\n* **Don't use `unsafe`.**\n* **Don't use `panic!` where `assert_eq!` / `assert!` work.**\n* **Don't transcribe C goto-ret tracking.**  Use early returns or\n  `?` propagation.\n* **Don't add `#[cfg(target_os = \"linux\")]` etc.** unless the C\n  body itself is OS-specific.\n* **Don't translate `picoquic_test_compare_text_files` golden-file\n  tests** without copying the reference file to `rs/fq/tests/fixtures/`\n  first.  Reach the path via\n  `concat!(env!(\"CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR\"), \"/tests/fixtures/<name>\")`.\n\n---\n\n## Known stubbed surface\n\nMost `Quic` / `Connection` / `Path` methods have signatures only —\ntheir bodies are `todo!()`.  Tests will panic on the first call.\nDon't try to verify behaviour against a working impl; the test is\na forward-looking spec for Phase 4.\n\nFunctions with **real bodies** today (will pass tests against\nthem):\n\n* `crate::VERSION` (constant)\n* `crate::internal::parse_16/24/32/64`, `format_16/24/32/64`\n* `crate::ConnectionId::{as_bytes, len, is_empty}`\n* `crate::stream::StreamId::{is_client, is_bidir, from_parts,\n  rank, kind, next_with_same_kind}`\n* `crate::frames::FrameType` discriminants (the variants exist,\n  even if `name()` is `todo!()`)\n* `crate::errors::{InternalError, TransportError}` discriminants\n* `crate::tests::util::TestSimPacket` / `TestSimLink` types\n  (signatures only)\n","numLines":347,"startLine":1,"totalLines":347}}}
