{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015E3G33DuxJKwYZaSVaXXxU","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[package]\n2\tname = \"fq\"\n3\tversion = \"0.1.0\"\n4\tedition = \"2024\"\n5\t\n6\t[features]\n7\tdefault = []\n8\t# Each backend lives behind its own feature so a binary only pays\n9\t# for the implementations it actually links.  See `src/sys/`.\n10\tsys-picotls = []\n11\tsys-openssl = [\"dep:openssl\"]\n12\tsys-mbedtls = []\n13\tsys-fusion = []\n14\t\n15\t[dependencies]\n16\tfugit = { version = \"0.3\", default-features = false }\n17\trand = { version = \"0.9\", default-features = false }\n18\trand_core = { version = \"0.9\", default-features = false }\n19\t\n20\t# Rust Crypto trait crates (no implementations -- those come from\n21\t# the active TLS backend's crypto layer, except for header\n22\t# protection which we implement ourselves).\n23\taead = { version = \"0.5\", default-features = false }\n24\tcipher = { version = \"0.4\", default-features = false }\n25\tdigest = { version = \"0.10\", default-features = false }\n26\t\n27\t# Concrete cipher implementations used by header protection\n28\t# (QUIC packet-number encryption is QUIC logic, not TLS).\n29\taes = { version = \"0.8\", default-features = false }\n30\tchacha20 = { version = \"0.9\", default-features = false }\n31\t\n32\t# UDP socket abstraction.  std-only.\n33\tsocket2 = { version = \"0.5\", default-features = false, features = [\"all\"] }\n34\t\n35\t# Optional backend implementations (gated by `sys-*` features).\n36\topenssl = { version = \"0.10\", optional = true }\n37\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cb85c5eb-b826-43b9-84a4-4be9b46756f2","uuid":"efa44648-2b2f-489e-8e2a-4e3c034b23ac","timestamp":"2026-05-05T11:55:03.526Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/richbarn/Projects/picoquic/rs/fq/Cargo.toml","content":"[package]\nname = \"fq\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\nedition = \"2024\"\n\n[features]\ndefault = []\n# Each backend lives behind its own feature so a binary only pays\n# for the implementations it actually links.  See `src/sys/`.\nsys-picotls = []\nsys-openssl = [\"dep:openssl\"]\nsys-mbedtls = []\nsys-fusion = []\n\n[dependencies]\nfugit = { version = \"0.3\", default-features = false }\nrand = { version = \"0.9\", default-features = false }\nrand_core = { version = \"0.9\", default-features = false }\n\n# Rust Crypto trait crates (no implementations -- those come from\n# the active TLS backend's crypto layer, except for header\n# protection which we implement ourselves).\naead = { version = \"0.5\", default-features = false }\ncipher = { version = \"0.4\", default-features = false }\ndigest = { version = \"0.10\", default-features = false }\n\n# Concrete cipher implementations used by header protection\n# (QUIC packet-number encryption is QUIC logic, not TLS).\naes = { version = \"0.8\", default-features = false }\nchacha20 = { version = \"0.9\", default-features = false }\n\n# UDP socket abstraction.  std-only.\nsocket2 = { version = \"0.5\", default-features = false, features = [\"all\"] }\n\n# Optional backend implementations (gated by `sys-*` features).\nopenssl = { version = \"0.10\", optional = true }\n","numLines":37,"startLine":1,"totalLines":37}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_012mmaouAr2R1u8F3iXwyCgY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"`socket2` is available. But I don't see `libc` in the dependencies. Let me check if we can use `libc::AF_INET` or if there's another way to get address family constants.\n\nActually, in socket2 crate, there's `socket2::Domain` which has `Domain::IPV4` and `Domain::IPV6`. But for our purposes, the C test uses `AF_INET = 2` and `AF_INET6 = 10`. Since we're on Linux/macOS, `libc::AF_INET` would be the right constant.\n\n\nWithout `libc` as a dependency, I need to find another way to handle the address family constants. Looking at how the C code sets the address family in the loop parameters, I should map the socket2 Domain types directly to the numeric values the struct expects.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":990,"cache_read_input_tokens":90920,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":990},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cb85c5eb-b826-43b9-84a4-4be9b46756f2","uuid":"7ad99811-2064-40bd-8734-c471ccc6895f"}
